Example two.

110
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,200
Thomas is always so belligerent.

111
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,380
It is impossible to talk to him.

112
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:25,320
Example three.

113
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:28,960
Stacey was fired for her belligerent attitude.

114
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,400
Okay.

115
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:36,840
So I can understand that it means sort of aggressive, having a strong willingness to fight.

116
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,560
Exactly.

117
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:42,360
A belligerent person, a belligerent attitude, a belligerent country.

118
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,360
Okay.

119
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,360
Very good.

120
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:45,280
And our last word for today.

121
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,160
Anguish.

122
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,120
Anguish.

123
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,920
Anguish.

124
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,200
So to cause great anguish.

125
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:55,080
To cause a lot of terrible emotional or physical pain.

126
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:55,640
Okay.

127
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,160
So it is a synonym of pain, of suffering.

128
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,160
Yeah.

129
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,100
But really intense suffering.

130
