157
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:12,850
Example one.

158
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:19,160
To finish this house, we need such materials as cement, wood, and steel.

159
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:25,480
Example two.

160
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:29,800
I need to write a report on a social topic such as psychology, health, or marriage.

161
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:33,820
Example three.

162
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:42,020
Companies have found that social networking sites such as Facebook and Twitter are great marketing opportunities.

163
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:49,500
So this is a really useful structure to use when you want to give examples of many different things.

164
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,280
Okay.

165
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:59,000
and as the alien was criticizing the humans, the guy said, what gives you the right to come and judge us?

166
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:00,800
So interesting phrase.

167
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,500
What gives you the right?

168
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,480
What gives you the right?

169
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:05,600
What gives you the right?

170
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:06,700
All right.

171
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:11,000
So if I tell you what gives you the right to, and then a verb.

172
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:12,400
Yeah.

173
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:13,400
What am I saying there?

174
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:16,780
You're basically saying you don't have the right to do this.

175
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:17,960
You shouldn't do this.

176
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:19,960
Why are you doing it?

177
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,680
Or why do you want to have this control over me?

178
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,080
Yep.

179
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,260
So when would you use this phrase?

180
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:36,840
If somebody is trying to control you or maybe somebody is judging you or doing something to you against your will, maybe, you would say, what gives you the right to take my phone away?

181
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,380
What gives you the right to tell me what to do?

182
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:40,340
All right.

183
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:44,420
It's a good phrase to tell that other person that they shouldn't do that.

184
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:45,580
They're doing something unfair.

185
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:46,300
Unfair.

186
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:46,640
Okay.

187
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,020
And our next phrase is very similar.

188
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:52,860
Who are you to play God with our fate?

189
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:53,760
Okay.

190
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:54,760
So I want to look at this.

191
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,360
To play God.

192
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:57,360
All right.

193
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:01,520
So to play God is making these arbitrary decisions.

194
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,780
Like he is the master of everything.

195
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,120
Right.

196
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,120
Controlling everything.

197
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:08,360
But this phrase, who are you to?

198
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:13,560
So basically saying you don't have the power or authority to do this.

199
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,760
And you can use it in exactly the same way.

200
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,120
Who are you to tell me what to do?

201
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,640
Who are you to take away my phone?

202
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:21,820
Exactly.

203
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:23,360
So you don't have the power to do this.

204
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,020
Very good.

205
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:28,660
So these phrases are a little bit aggressive, almost belligerent, wouldn't you say?

206
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:29,780
A little bit.

207
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:38,540
But I guess if you are being treated unfair or if you are angry at a situation, it would be a good phrase to use to put your point across.

208
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:38,940
Yes.

209
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:41,860
And as we saw, these humans are pretty angry.

210
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:48,200
So why don't we listen again as they're telling the aliens, who are you to do this to us?

211
00:10:48,640 --> 00:11:00,320
Oh, honey, this is so romantic.

212
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:03,800
I have never seen like so many stars before.

213
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,210
It's beautiful.

214
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:06,330
See that constellation there?

215
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:07,730
That's Orion.

216
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:09,810
And the very bright star?

217
00:11:10,450 --> 00:11:12,430
Well, it's not a star because it doesn't blink.

218
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:14,230
That's actually Venus.

219
00:11:15,590 --> 00:11:19,090
What's that big, flashy one?

220
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:20,710
I don't know.

221
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:22,510
I think it's a UFO.

222
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,160
Greetings, Earthlings.

223
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:41,360
I come from afar, from a distant galaxy known only to a few.

224
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:42,820
Why are you here?

225
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:45,020
Where did you come from?

226
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,180
We have been observing you for the last three thousand years.

227
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:56,460
We have seen your amazing capacity that humans have to create such wonders as the Taj Mahal or masterpieces such as the Hafner Symphony.

228
00:11:57,280 --> 00:12:00,780
Unfortunately, your intelligence and creativity does not come without consequence.

229
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:05,660
Your ambition and desire for more will be your downfall, and we are here to save your planet from you.

230
00:12:06,930 --> 00:12:08,550
You think you have us figured out?

231
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:11,130
What gives you the right to come and judge us?

232
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:13,710
Who are you to play God with our fate?

233
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,160
Silence, human.

234
00:12:16,150 --> 00:12:19,930
It is that belligerent attitude that has caused years of pain and anguish among yourselves.

235
00:12:20,350 --> 00:12:21,250
Now you will pay the price.

236
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:48,700
Okay so UFOs and constellations and stars and planets.

